<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blida</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blida is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> at the foot of the Tell <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas</a>, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>, on the edge of the Mitidja plain. Founded in the 16th century, it was occupied by the French during the conquest of Algeria in the 1830s and grew into a garrison and market town. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frantz-fanon">Frantz Fanon</a> worked at its psychiatric hospital in the 1950s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blida.jpg" alt="Blida" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BullyanDZ · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chrea_blida_snow.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
